---
import FaqBlock from "../../components/FaqBlock.astro";
import ContentFigure from "../../components/ContentFigure.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";
import { articleSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema, graph, websiteSchema } from "../../lib/schema";
import { getNhcCurrentFeed } from "../../lib/nhcCurrent";
import { getAtlanticOutlook } from "../../lib/nhcOutlook";

const { feed } = await getNhcCurrentFeed();
const atlanticStorms = feed.storms.filter((storm) => /^AL/i.test(storm.id ?? ""));
const primaryAtlanticStorm = atlanticStorms[0];
const primaryAtlanticSlug = String(primaryAtlanticStorm?.name ?? primaryAtlanticStorm?.id ?? "storm").toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/^-|-$/g, "");
const outlook = await getAtlanticOutlook();
const title = "Tropical Disturbance Tracker | Atlantic Formation Outlook";
const description = "Track Atlantic tropical disturbances, NHC formation outlook areas, current named storms, and the difference between an outlook area, Invest, and forecast track.";
const url = `${site.url}/hurricane-tracker/tropical-disturbances/`;
const lastModified = "2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z";
const faqs = [
  { question: "What is a tropical disturbance?", answer: "A tropical disturbance is an area of organized tropical weather that may or may not develop into a tropical cyclone. It is not automatically a depression, named storm, or hurricane." },
  { question: "Does an NHC outlook area show where a storm will travel?", answer: "No. An outlook area shows where development could occur during the outlook period. It is not a forecast cone, storm track, warning area, or impact boundary." },
  { question: "What is an Invest?", answer: "An Invest is a numbered system used by operational weather centers to organize additional data collection and model analysis. Not every disturbance receives an Invest number, and not every Invest becomes a named storm." },
  { question: "Where can I track a disturbance after it is named?", answer: "Once NHC lists a named tropical cyclone, open its HurricaneHub named-storm page and verify all forecasts and watches with the official NHC advisory." }
];
const jsonLd = graph(websiteSchema(), articleSchema({ title, description, url, dateModified: lastModified }), faqSchema(faqs), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: "Home", url: site.canonicalUrl }, { name: "Live Hurricane Tracker", url: `${site.url}/hurricane-tracker/live/` }, { name: "Tropical Disturbances", url }]));
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={url} jsonLd={jsonLd} lastModified={lastModified}>
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="disturbance-title"><div class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">Official NHC formation outlook</p><h1 id="disturbance-title">Tropical Disturbance Tracker</h1><p class="answer">Monitor Atlantic development areas before a storm receives a name. Use the NHC seven-day outlook for formation potential, then move to the live hurricane tracker when NHC begins issuing cyclone advisories.</p><p class="section-actions"><a class="action-link" href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/gtwo.php" rel="noopener nofollow">Open official NHC outlook</a><a class="action-link secondary-action" href="/hurricane-tracker/live/">Open live hurricane tracker</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="atlantic-outlook"><div class="inner grid-2"><article><p class="eyebrow">Atlantic basin</p><h2 id="atlantic-outlook">Seven-Day Formation Outlook Map</h2><p>The map uses NHC development probabilities. Colored regions identify where a tropical cyclone could form, not where an eventual storm would travel or cause impacts.</p><p class="source-note">Current named Atlantic systems: {atlanticStorms.length ? atlanticStorms.map((storm) => storm.name).filter(Boolean).join(", ") : "none"}. Pacific systems are listed on the <a href="/hurricane-tracker/live/">all-basin live tracker</a>. Feed checked {feed.updatedAt}.</p></article><article class="panel outlook-map"><img src="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/xgtwo/two_atl_7d0.png" width="900" height="679" loading="eager" alt="Official NHC seven-day Atlantic tropical weather outlook map" /></article></div></section>
  {outlook && <section class="band" aria-labelledby="outlook-text"><div class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">Current official outlook · {outlook.issued}</p><h2 id="outlook-text">Atlantic Disturbances NHC Is Monitoring</h2><p class="answer">{outlook.text}</p>{(outlook.formationChance48h != null || outlook.formationChance7d != null) && <p><strong>Current formation chance:</strong> {outlook.formationChance48h ?? "—"}% within 48 hours · {outlook.formationChance7d ?? "—"}% within 7 days.</p>}<p class="section-actions">{primaryAtlanticStorm && <a class="action-link" href={`/hurricane-tracker/storm/${primaryAtlanticSlug}/`}>Track {primaryAtlanticStorm.name ?? "active storm"}</a>}<a class:list={["action-link", primaryAtlanticStorm && "secondary-action"]} href="/hurricane-tracker/gulf/">Open Gulf hurricane tracker</a><a class="action-link secondary-action" href="/tracker/florida/">Florida tracker</a><a class="action-link secondary-action" href="/tracker/louisiana/">Louisiana tracker</a></p><p class="source-note"><a href={outlook.source} rel="noopener nofollow">Read the official NHC Atlantic Tropical Weather Outlook</a>. {primaryAtlanticStorm ? `${primaryAtlanticStorm.name ?? "The listed system"} has a separate storm tracker; check its classification and advisory source for continuing hazards. This outlook also covers additional formation areas.` : "An outlook area or Invest is not yet a tropical depression or named storm, and its formation probability is not a track, warning area, or impact forecast."}</p></div></section>}
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="disturbance-terms"><div class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">Development terms</p><h2 id="disturbance-terms">Disturbance, Invest, Depression, and Named Storm</h2><ContentFigure src="/images/guides/tropical-development-stages.svg" alt="Outlook, Invest, depression and named-storm terms, with a Potential Tropical Cyclone exception allowing advisories before formation" caption="These are not mandatory sequential stages. An outlook area or Invest may never develop; NHC can issue Potential Tropical Cyclone advisories before a tropical cyclone forms." /><div class="grid-2 section-grid"><article class="panel"><h3>Tropical Disturbance</h3><p>An area of unsettled tropical weather. Formation probability can rise or fall without a cyclone forming.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Invest</h3><p>An operational identifier such as 90L used to organize observations and model analysis. It is not a storm classification and does not by itself establish that watches or warnings have been issued.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Tropical Depression</h3><p>A closed tropical circulation with maximum sustained winds below tropical-storm strength. It receives official advisories and a forecast track; those products may already have begun under a Potential Tropical Cyclone designation.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Named Tropical Storm or Hurricane</h3><p>A classified tropical cyclone with a name and recurring official advisory package. Use its dedicated tracker page for current status.</p></article></div><h3>Potential Tropical Cyclone: Advisories Before Formation</h3><p>NHC uses this term for a disturbance that is not yet a tropical cyclone but threatens tropical-storm or hurricane conditions over land within 72 hours. It allows advisory products, including a forecast track and applicable watches or warnings, before formation. It is not a guarantee that the disturbance will become a named storm. Read the actual advisory and local instructions rather than waiting for a depression or name.</p><p class="source-note">Definition checked November 9, 2026 against the <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/aboutgloss.shtml" rel="noopener nofollow">NHC Potential Tropical Cyclone glossary entry</a>. This explains terminology, not a current threat.</p></div></section>
  <FaqBlock faqs={faqs} />
</Layout>
<style>.outlook-map img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px}</style>
